    "summary": "Strong Eyes of the World → Stella Blue transition and solid second set",
    "blurb": "Features a standout Eyes Of The World into Stella Blue transition, strong Dark Star pairings, and solid performances of Brown Eyed Women and Stella Blue. Jerry delivers concise solos while Phil’s bass shines throughout. Good soundboard capture with occasional drop‑outs makes it a recommended listen for ’73 fans.",
    "review": "The Assembly Hall show on February 21, 1973 captures the Dead in a tight groove as they navigate a classic early‑’70s setlist. Set two opens with the familiar China Cat > I Know You Rider before moving into a crisp Jack Straw and Mississippi Half-Step Uptown Toodeloo, but it’s the Truckin' tease that launches into an expansive Eyes Of The World jam. Jerry Garcia offers a concise, melodic solo after the jam, handing the floor to Phil Lesh for a powerful bass‑driven solo that propels the band straight into a heartfelt Stella Blue. The second half of the set keeps the momentum with Sugar Magnolia and Casey Jones, while the encore’s Johnny B. Goode adds a fun close. Both available soundboard recordings are clear enough to enjoy the nuances, though listeners should be aware of occasional drop‑outs that prevent an immaculate listening experience.",
